<section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Continuous emotional care intelligence</p><h1>Support for the part that comes <em>after.</em></h1><p class="lede">Chiedza listens, notices patterns, adapts to emotional capacity, and connects people to human care when self-guided support is not enough.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/register">Enter Chiedza</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/about">See how care is routed</a></div><p class="microcopy">No streaks. No guilt. No infinite feed. AI is disclosed and does not replace licensed care.</p></div><div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="lantern-scene"><div class="lantern-glow"></div><div class="lantern-frame"><div class="lantern-flame"></div></div><div class="lantern-reflection"></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section intro-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">The recovery gap</p><h2>Healthcare often ends before recovery does.</h2></div><div><p>Chiedza is designed as a recovery layer that can sit alongside therapists, healthcare providers, employers, universities, schools, insurers and governments rather than replacing them.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The Quiet Arcade</p><h2>Five rooms. One manageable action at a time.</h2></div><div class="card-grid five"><article class="room-card calm"><span>01</span><h3>Calm Me</h3><p>Lantern Breathing for panic, overwhelm and racing thoughts.</p></article><article class="room-card ground"><span>02</span><h3>Ground Me</h3><p>A sensory Quiet Room for anxiety or feeling far away.</p></article><article class="room-card rest"><span>03</span><h3>Let Me Rest</h3><p>The Long Afternoon. No task. No aftercare. The room is the aftercare.</p></article><article class="room-card return"><span>04</span><h3>Help Me Return</h3><p>The Memory House for grief, identity and reintegration.</p></article><article class="room-card carry"><span>05</span><h3>Carry With Me</h3><p>Anonymous slow community without likes, replies or followers.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section dark-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">Care orchestration</p><h2>AI listens. Humans retain authority.</h2></div><div class="route-list"><div><span>Stable</span><strong>AI support only</strong></div><div><span>Struggling</span><strong>Therapist suggestion</strong></div><div><span>Overwhelmed</span><strong>Reduce stimulation + grounding</strong></div><div><span>High Risk</span><strong>Urgent human alert</strong></div><div><span>Crisis</span><strong>Emergency protocol</strong></div></div></section>
